Hello Teya Partner Team,

Thank you again for setting up our sandbox store. We have now built Teya into=
 Vesopa EPOS end to end - card machines on the tills and online payments on o=
ur table-ordering menu - and run the scenarios in your "Test Your Integration=
" checklist on the sandbox. We would like to begin partner certification.

If this is better handled by your partner technology or integrations team, pl=
ease forward this on, or point me to the right contact and I will pick it up =
from there.

OUR ACCOUNT
- Company: Vesopa Software Ltd (Vesopa EPOS, UK hospitality ePOS)
- Sandbox login: muzahid@vesopa.com (partner.teya.xyz and the sandbox sign-in)
- Device Code application: Client ID c8fb0c2a-081e-49e5-83d2-76731652f1c8
- Web application: Client ID be31f2c2-93b6-4074-b472-c5f2fce3ccc8
- Test store: "Vesopa" (b5244164-f4e7-4a85-b3df-ddc1ded9fefc), card machine "=
OTHER"

POSLINK: TESTED ON THE SANDBOX
- Install and start the SDK: Vesopa EPOS downloads and runs the Teya SDK app =
1.9.0 as a sub-process over JSON-RPC, checks the signing certificate first, a=
nd initialises on the sandbox.
- Authenticate the merchant: Device Code flow with our credentials; the back =
office then lists the store's card machines and lets each till pick its machi=
ne.
- Make a payment: makePaymentAndSubscribe with the live state changes shown o=
n the till (present card, PIN, approved).
- Cancel a payment: cancelPayment during an in-progress payment, with the res=
ult reflected on the till.
- Refund: full and partial refundPayment back to the card, by the gateway pay=
ment id.
- Lost connection: COMMUNICATION_FAILED and no answer are shown as =E2=80=9Cn=
ot confirmed=E2=80=9D with a check-the-machine prompt, never as declined.
- Pay at counter: once Cloud communication is enabled on the machine (Setting=
s > POS integrations > External ePOS integrations), the machine actions the e=
POS request as your guide describes.

ONLINE PAYMENTS: TESTED ON THE SANDBOX
- Hosted checkout for our table-ordering menu, with plugin registration (plug=
inType TESTING), a signed registration webhook and payments webhook, and onli=
ne refunds - all working on the sandbox.

WHAT WE WOULD LIKE TO AGREE
1. Begin certification for POSLink (card machines) and for Online Payments. P=
lease point us at the certification checklist or test script you would like u=
s to evidence, or book a certification call.
2. Production credentials: when should we request the live Device Code and we=
b application credentials, and our own pluginType for online payments (in pla=
ce of TESTING)?
3. Our physical card machine: Teya has delivered a live card machine for our =
test venue. Is there anything you need from us to approve it for live ePOS pa=
yments once certified?
4. Go-live: the steps and any paperwork to move a venue from sandbox to live =
once certification passes.

We can share a short screen recording of each scenario, or run them live with=
 you on a call - whichever your certification process prefers. We are ready t=
o go whenever you are.

Many thanks for your help.

Kind regards,
Muzahid Islam
Vesopa Developer, Vesopa Software Ltd
muzahid@vesopa.com

On behalf of Meirion Davies, Director
Vesopa Software Ltd and Vesopa Ltd
info@vesopasoftware.com | info@vesopa.com

